This source package repackages the tagged release artifacts rather than
compiling from source.

The upstream/ directory contains the installed trees extracted from the
release .deb files, per architecture:

  upstream/yunmai-noble/amd64/...
  upstream/yunmai-noble/arm64/...
  upstream/yunmai-noble-desktop/{amd64,arm64}/...
  upstream/yunmai-noble-simulator/{amd64,arm64}/...
  upstream/yunmai-noble-full/all/...

Those trees include the bundled Bun runtime, the GPUI binaries built by the
release workflow, vendored production node_modules, the web UI, systemd units,
and conffiles. debian/rules installs the tree that matches DEB_HOST_ARCH.

The binaries are prebuilt and are not rebuilt on Launchpad. That is acceptable
for a PPA; it would not be acceptable for the Debian or Ubuntu archives.
